  "segment": "bootstrap-config",
  "source_text": "Arbiter uses Hydra as its configuration framework. Hydra composes the config object Arbiter uses from YAML files in the conf directory and validates those files with schemas provided by Arbiter and its plugins. Arbiter provides bootstrap commands that create initial config files you can edit to match your needs. First, create the server config. Then bootstrap IMAP and SMTP account and policy templates. These files are starting points; edit them to match your accounts, folders, and policy boundaries.",
